// The field layer, third pass, part "collision" (Phase 5 slice `field3`; docs/ANALYSIS/26_field.md section 4): the
// k_fldFrame.c band 0x1AA8F0-0x1AFD40 -- the collision controller task and its primitives, the sphere-vs-world
// contact gatherers, the ground ray, the transparent-wall pickers, the move / turn helpers on a controller, and the
// "collis mover" / "collis sphere" / "death se" tasks. Generated by p3fes_handgen (one statement per instruction on
// the hg_cpu register view: frame, spills, $ra links, cycle charges and check points exactly as the recompiled bodies)
// and made readable on top -- roles, named offsets, block comments, host-side structure; nothing that runs was moved.
// Pair tests: tests/game/test_field3_collision.cpp.
//
// The records (offsets from the instructions; names are ours, ADR-0009):
//  * the collision controller work (52 bytes, K_FldFrame_CreateCtlTask; 26_field.md 4.2): +0 state (0 = a move is
//    pending, 1 = idle, 2 = off), +4 flags (bit 31 debug sphere, bit 30 snap to the ground, bit 28 no collision,
//    bit 27 frozen), +8 u16 scene resource id, +10 u16 the field unit's id, +12 the field unit, +16 the model,
//    +20..+28 f32 the pending displacement, +32 f32 the sphere radius (also the height of the collision centre),
//    +36 zeroed, +40 s32 accumulated distance, +44 / +48 s32 the 800-unit grid cell x / z.
//  * the sphere-contact record (on the caller's stack, 2,872 bytes; sub_1AB390 / sub_1ABD20 build it, the triangle
//    callbacks sub_1AAF30 / sub_1AB640 fill it): +0 [64] vec3 the contact points, +768 [64] vec3 the contact
//    triangles' normals (the key that merges contacts of one plane), +1536 [64] f32 the distance of each contact
//    (initialised to the $gp constant 0x7CAEFC, "far"), +2560 [64] u32 "met while gathering the moving models", +2816
//    the gathering flag, +2820 s32 the contact count, +2824 s32 the flagged count, +2828 vec3 the normalised step,
//    +2840 a 7-word copy of the sphere intersection (centre, radius, .., type 3), +2868 the atomic being tested,
//    +2872 vec3 zeroed.
//  * the RW intersection (RpIntersection as the callers lay it out: vec3 + f32 at +0..+12, type at +24: 1 = line,
//    3 = sphere) and the line-query record of sub_1ACB70 / sub_1ACC30 ({+0 the result vec3 pointer, +4 hit flag,
//    +8.. the intersection, +36 f32 the best t, +40 the atomic}).
//  * the "collis mover" work (1,440 bytes, sub_1AF930): +4 flags (bit 31 debug markers), +12 the scene resource it
//    moves, +16 its kind (resource +296 -> +214, high byte), +24 the mode (0 = the waypoint queue, 1 = the second
//    queue), +28 the queue count (at most 47) of 24-byte entries at +32 {+0 kind, +4 vec3 target, +16 f32 speed,
//    +20 the debug-marker task}, +1204 a state word (5 for non-character resources), +1228 an RW object freed at
//    destroy, +1240 the second queue's count (at most 7) of 24-byte entries at +1248 {vec3, f32}.
//
// Left recompiled on purpose: sub_1AB390 [K_FldFrame_CollideWorld], sub_1ABD20 [K_FldFrame_CollideClump] and
// sub_1AD9E0 [K_FldFrame_CtlSetOrientation] -- tests/game/test_field_big.cpp pairs their callers up to the call into
// them as not-emitted callees (stop pc and registers there), so replacing them would break that slice's checks.
#include "p3fes/game/hg_cpu.h"
#include "p3fes/game/field3_collision.h"

